module std where

-- =========================================================================
-- Nat (Peano) arithmetic — the PURE source of truth (numeric-tower Phase 1).
--
-- These bodies are the conceptual definition of natural-number arithmetic
-- over the pure ADT `Nat = Zero | Succ pred:Nat` (type-foundation.ts:551 /
-- fenel/std/foundation.fenel). They are the SEMANTICS that the flat
-- `@native` `add`/`mul`/`sub`/`div`/`mod`/`lt`/`eq` over the opaque `number`
-- repr (math-native.fenel / logic-native.fenel + json-logic.ts) are the
-- runtime performance branch FOR, and that the compile DirectOp lowering
-- (`add→F64Add` … lower-to-wasm-ast.fenel:82 / lower-to-llvm-ast.fenel:98)
-- is the compiled performance branch FOR. The D7 round-trip law (numeric-
-- tower notes/phase-0-audit.md §3) binds all three: for x,y in the opaque
-- `number` rep, `natToNumber (natOp (numberToNat x) (numberToNat y))` agrees
-- with the native and the DirectOp result. [[feedback_opaque_is_optimization]]
--
-- POSITIONAL SURFACE (representation-substrate Phase 2 — the construct-gap
-- dissolution). These bodies now construct + destructure `Succ` via the
-- POSITIONAL surface (`Succ x` / `case n of Succ p -> …`), retiring the
-- numeric-tower Phase-1 NAMED-FIELD workaround (`Succ { pred = x }`). The gap
-- that forced the workaround — `Nat`'s `Zero`/`Succ` were unindexed because
-- `Nat` was not a registered entity, so the `construct` op corrupted a
-- positional payload — is GONE: Phase 1 taught the registry `$opaque`-peel to
-- index an opaque type's pure `$variant` cases (registry.ts), and Phase 2
-- registers `Nat` as a catalog entity (the `@label`/`@description` on its
-- `foundation.fenel` decl ⇒ the `foundationEntityRegs` auto-loop registers it).
-- So `_constructors.Succ = ["pred"]` is now populated, and positional `Succ x`
-- builds the canonical `{$tag:"Succ", _0:x}` (positional binds by ORDER to
-- `_0`, NOT the declared field name — json-logic.ts:1019, the std-lib `Just x`
-- ≡ `{_0:x}` convention; the parser lowers positional patterns the same way,
-- fenel-parser.ts:1657). Build + match are self-consistent on `_0`. ZERO new
-- TS — the dissolution is pure `.fenel` (the foundation directive) over the
-- live Phase-1 peel.
--
-- These are NEW, standalone, Nat-typed fnIds (`std:natAdd` …). They are NOT
-- added to `stdNatives`/`BUILTIN_OP_NATIVES` (the D1 shadow trap), NOT given
-- a `defineFunction` TS spec, and do NOT change the `Number` natives or the
-- DirectOp lowering (D2/D7 fences). Phase 5's `Numeric Nat` instance's `add`
-- method body will REFERENCE `natAdd` (the names are stable).

@label "Nat add"
@description "Peano addition over Nat = Zero | Succ. Structural recursion on the first operand: natAdd Zero b = b; natAdd (Succ p) b = Succ (natAdd p b). The pure source of truth for `add` at the Nat rung."
@tags "numeric" "nat" "peano"
natAdd : (a: Nat) -> (b: Nat) -> Nat
natAdd a b = case a of
  Zero -> b
  Succ p -> Succ (natAdd p b)

@label "Nat multiply"
@description "Peano multiplication as repeated addition: natMul Zero b = Zero; natMul (Succ p) b = natAdd b (natMul p b). Composes natAdd."
@tags "numeric" "nat" "peano"
natMul : (a: Nat) -> (b: Nat) -> Nat
natMul a b = case a of
  Zero -> Zero
  Succ p -> natAdd b (natMul p b)

@label "Nat monus"
@description "Truncated subtraction (monus) — the Nat counterpart of `sub`: natMonus n Zero = n; natMonus Zero _ = Zero; natMonus (Succ p) (Succ q) = natMonus p q. Total (never negative); a-b clamps to Zero when b > a. Int (Phase 2) makes subtraction total/signed."
@tags "numeric" "nat" "peano"
natMonus : (a: Nat) -> (b: Nat) -> Nat
natMonus a b = case b of
  Zero -> a
  Succ q -> case a of
    Zero -> Zero
    Succ p -> natMonus p q

@label "Nat less-than"
@description "Structural strict order over Nat: natLt a Zero = False; natLt Zero (Succ _) = True; natLt (Succ p) (Succ q) = natLt p q. Total (Nat order is decidable; the ℝ rung is where eq/lt go partial, D4)."
@tags "numeric" "nat" "peano" "comparison"
natLt : (a: Nat) -> (b: Nat) -> Boolean
natLt a b = case b of
  Zero -> False
  Succ q -> case a of
    Zero -> True
    Succ p -> natLt p q

@label "Nat equal"
@description "Structural equality over Nat: both Zero ⇒ True; one Zero ⇒ False; both Succ ⇒ recurse on the predecessors. Total. The pure source of truth for `eq` at the Nat rung (the D6 String-typed native eq is fixed under the Eq class at Phase 5, not here)."
@tags "numeric" "nat" "peano" "comparison"
natEq : (a: Nat) -> (b: Nat) -> Boolean
natEq a b = case a of
  Zero -> case b of
    Zero -> True
    Succ q -> False
  Succ p -> case b of
    Zero -> False
    Succ q -> natEq p q

@label "Nat divide"
@description "Truncated (floor) division as repeated monus, guarded by natLt: natDiv a b = if a < b then Zero else Succ (natDiv (a - b) b). Zero divisor returns Zero (mirrors the native's zero-guard-to-0; the D7 law is asserted over the non-zero-divisor domain — the exact/refined-divisor semantics land at the Rational rung). Terminates by a well-founded Nat measure (the dividend strictly decreases while b >= 1) which is below the totality checker's structural/sub-1 rungs ⇒ checker returns Unknown, NOT @partial (the body IS total)."
@tags "numeric" "nat" "peano"
natDiv : (a: Nat) -> (b: Nat) -> Nat
natDiv a b = case b of
  Zero -> Zero
  Succ q -> if natLt a b then Zero else Succ (natDiv (natMonus a b) b)

@label "Nat modulo"
@description "Remainder via repeated monus, guarded by natLt: natMod a b = if a < b then a else natMod (a - b) b. Zero divisor returns a (keeps the div/mod identity a = b*(a/b) + a%b with natDiv a Zero = Zero; this DIVERGES from the native's zero-guard-to-0 — the documented zero-divisor carve-out, D7). Total by the same Nat measure as natDiv ⇒ checker Unknown, not @partial."
@tags "numeric" "nat" "peano"
natMod : (a: Nat) -> (b: Nat) -> Nat
natMod a b = case b of
  Zero -> a
  Succ q -> if natLt a b then a else natMod (natMonus a b) b
